  bootwright / controller install
      Prepare this host's context-independent controller prerequisites: the baseline host
      packages, installed through the host's own dnf, and the controller runtime, a venv on the
      OS Python holding exactly the wheels this build locks and carries, so it downloads no
      wheel. This command selects no context; the prerequisites a context adds are installed by
      the controller stage of apply. A ready host makes no request and no change. Otherwise the
      plan shows dnf's own preview before confirmation. --dry-run never elevates: it names the
      host package requirements without a preview and makes no changes, and --dry-run --output
      json or --output yaml also lists every locked wheel's file, URL and SHA-256. Review the
      plan before confirming; --yes skips ordinary confirmation.

  Usage
    bootwright controller install [flags]

  Command flags
      --dry-run  Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --yes      Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright controller install --dry-run
